# The runtime of Ruby SDKs generated by tungsten (the `tungsten-runtime`
# gem): standard library only (net/http, json, openssl, securerandom).
#
# A generated SDK is mostly data, its SDK descriptor document
# (`tungsten-descriptors.json`), plus thin typed methods; everything with
# behaviour lives here, so every operation behaves the same way, and the
# same way as the TypeScript, Python, Rust and Go runtimes.
#
# Tungsten::Runtime::ClientCore runs each call through one pipeline:
# pre-flight validation of the arguments, auth (bearer with a required
# prefix, API keys, basic, composite profiles, OAuth2 client credentials and
# authorization code), idempotency keys, the confirmation rules of
# destructive operations, sending with tier-aware retries, and the
# classification of the answer (or of a lost request) into Ok or Err
# carrying the diagnostic envelope. On top of it: previews with
# confirmation tokens, verification hooks, pagination, polling, macros and
# server-sent event streams. Calls are synchronous; nothing raises for an
# API or transport failure.
module Tungsten
  # See Tungsten::Runtime::ClientCore.
  module Runtime
  end
end

